landing-review: vulkan-only plan, landing 11-1 -- the Direct3D9 renderer goes

Range reviewed: main...HEAD at 6de89fb (0470c2b..6de89fb after the 10c-3
landing; the code half is 3f71759 alone, 13 files). The branch moved
under the reviewer and it said so: 6de89fb was docs-only and it read
both. Commits added AFTER the review: 816fb2b and 5cb58c3 (docs, landing
11-2's forward survey) and ec41026 (this landing's own fix commit).
Reviewer: dedicated read-only agent, `medium` (CLAUDE.md: touches
tagpu/ddraw/**; it writes no engine state, moves no byte patch and
changes no game-thread/render-thread synchronisation, so not `high`).
ONE round. No HIGH.

WHAT LANDED. The Direct3D9 backend, whole: render_d3d9.c (742),
render_d3d9.h (50), d3d9shader.h (1595), and every d3d9_* call site in
dd.c, config.c, debug.c, dllmain.c, utils.c, winapi_hooks.c and
wndproc.c. 2 538 lines out, 34 in, 13 files. It is the one member of the
plan's deletion set with no producer half -- `git grep -i d3d9 main --
'tagpu/ddraw/src/tagpu_*' 'tagpu/ddraw/inc/tagpu_*'` is empty, so no pass
of ours and no Vulkan entry point ever touched it.

Landing 11 also split into five parts here, which the row had needed
since the surveys: 11-1 the renderer-selection surface, 11-2 the world
passes' GL draw halves, 11-3 the UI and support passes', 11-4 the GL
entry-point surface itself (and with it `tacli shot`/`glshot`, wired only
into render_ogl.c), 11-5 the exit condition. The definitional call the
row was told to make is made: the exit condition is stock as a LANE.

WHAT THE REVIEWER VERIFIED, and this was the risk in the change. The two
"identity" simplifications hold on every arm, checked against main and
not against the post-deletion tree. `BOOL d3d9_active` was assigned in
exactly two places, each inside `if (renderer == d3d9_render_main)`, and
initialised FALSE in each -- so for gdi, ogl and vk it was invariably
FALSE, `!d3d9_active || nonexclusive` was always true, and the block that
now runs unconditionally is the one all three already took. The deleted
`d3d9_active && nonexclusive` reset was unreachable on a surviving lane;
the windowed branch's copy was assigned and never read. wndproc.c's two
`renderer != d3d9_render_main || nonexclusive` tests are exactly `if (1)`
now, at both the activate and deactivate sites, so window placement,
mouse locking and display-mode restore are unchanged. Also verified: the
new inline fopen is not under the loader lock (dd_CreateEx is reached
from the exported DirectDrawCreate* and the CoCreateInstance hook, never
DllMain), g_config.renderer is a bounded char[256] and is the argument
rather than the format, and <stdio.h> was genuinely absent before.

FINDINGS, ALL ACTED ON IN ec41026.
 - MEDIUM: three wrong figures in one sentence. The code half is 13
   files / 34 added / 2 538 deleted; 2 539, 119 and sixteen are the whole
   commit including the notes.
 - MEDIUM: gpu-status attributed 2 539 lines to the three deleted files,
   which are 2 387.
 - MEDIUM: `renderer=auto` -- what the generated ini writes, so the
   default a release-zip player gets -- read `!IsWine() &&
   d3d9_is_available()` first and selected Direct3D9 on native Windows.
   It now goes straight to OpenGL. Under Wine that branch was never
   taken, so nothing on the reference setup moved and no measurement here
   touches it. Recorded as the gap it is.
 - LOW: pre-deletion survey paragraphs left reading as present tense in
   the same document that marks 11-1 done; now marked as the survey they
   are. inc/vulkan/README.md no longer cites d3d9shader.h.
 - LOW: config/ConfigFormUnit.cpp, the upstream C++ Builder settings GUI,
   is the one surviving writer of the d3d9_filter key and still offers
   "Direct3D 9". Not built by the Makefile and already stale against this
   fork (no vulkan entry either), so it is named in "what was
   deliberately left" rather than edited.
 - LOW/NIT: the vcxproj and its filters named deleted files (both
   unmaintained here -- the Makefile globs and needed no change); two
   sites left half-simplified are collapsed the way the other four were;
   inc/dd.h's four FILTER_* defines now have no user and are named.

MEASURED. openglcore, vulkan and gdi each launch, draw and answer
`tacli ui`; an instance whose ini still asks for the deleted lane gets
GDI and one log line. The GL lane was additionally taken in-game through
a scenario load with the world drawing and `tacli roster` answering.

WHAT IS NOT COVERED. The `auto` path on native Windows, which cannot be
exercised here at all -- _local/vm/ is the kit for it and is waiting on
the owner. A release carrying this change says so in its notes.

AND A RETRACTION THIS LANDING CARRIES FOR THE PREVIOUS ONE. 10c-3's note
on 76077e4 recorded a second run as gdi and concluded the roster
keepalive's force is only a floor on the fill rate. That run was on
OpenGL: `tacli scenario load` calls write_ddraw_ini whenever the scenario
carries a setup.res, and it writes renderer=openglcore unconditionally,
so the hand-set renderer=gdi did not survive. 76077e4's note now carries
the retraction and the harness trap is written up in the ta-drive skill.
